sentences.t:
“Coniugio, Anchise, Veneris dignate superbo,
cura deum, bis Pergameis erepte ruinis,
ecce tibi Ausoniae tellus;

sentences.l:
“Of wedlock, Anchises, of Venus proud, deemed worthy,
care of gods, twice from Pergamean ruins snatched,
lo, for you Ausonia's land;

sentences.t:
Epiro, Hesperia, quibus idem Dardanus auctor
atque idem casus, unam faciemus utramque
Troiam animis;

sentences.l:
in Epirus, in Hesperia, to whom the same Dardanus founder
and the same fate, one we shall make each
Troy in spirit;
